## 2. Methods
This review followed the PRISMA (Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses) guidelines, systematically identifying and appraising peer-reviewed RCTs reporting on the effect of Vitamin D supplementation for individuals with symptoms of depression with the objectives of investigating:
*   the primary evidence for Vitamin D supplementation and depression from RCTs;

*   the types of subjects, the dose of Vitamin D supplementation, the control interventions and the measures of outcome used;

*   methodological quality of the studies;

*   biological flaws in the study design, and

*   estimates of the size of the effect.
